            <ArticleTitle>Retinal meteor.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>879-881</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/ijo.IJO_68_17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of a 65-year old man diagnosed with retinal vasoproliferative tumour secondary to posterior uveitis. The fluorescein angiography shows an interesting meteor-like leak emanating from the tumour and rising towards the superior retina in the later frames of the angiogram. Pictorially, we call it the &quot;Retinal Meteor&quot; and also describe the possible mechanism for this pattern of leakage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
